{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi","id":10962,"title":"Anubi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-14T18:23:35-08:00","id":10962,"title":"Anubi?","content":"I don't know if there were any definitive answer on the WW forums about this, but are there any plans on publishing the splat for the Gangrel bloodline Anubi anytime soon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">R<i>emember, remember, the Fifth of November, the Gunpowder Treason and Plot. I know of no reason why the Gunpowder Treason should ever be forgot.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> -V for Vendetta</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/997-japheth","name":"Japheth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar997_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"122"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:23:42-07:00","id":549638,"title":"","content":"I was looking to resurrect the Anubi from Milwaukee by Night into my chronicle of VtR, I see them as a Gangrel bloodline on the interactive character sheet, but no real information in the books I have. I would like to know if they are detailed in any VtR books and if so which one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4380-blunt_force_trauma","name":"Blunt_Force_Trauma","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T21:16:53-07:00","id":549741,"title":"","content":"No, they are mentioned in passing in the VtR 1e core book, but that's it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T00:46:04-07:00","id":549865,"title":"","content":"As I recall, the Anubi are described as staunchly pagan and martial in outlook, so I imagine they might be somewhat similar to the Childer of the Morrigan from the Circle of the Crone book. Unfortunately, that's not terribly helpful in 2E, since the Childer don't really have anything that could be interpreted as a Bloodline Gift. If I were to design them, I'd probably give them some kind of unique fighting style merit. Maybe I'll work something up when I'm more awake...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T09:49:24-07:00","id":550265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=549865#post549865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, the Anubi are described as staunchly pagan and martial in outlook, so I imagine they might be somewhat similar to the Childer of the Morrigan from the Circle of the Crone book. Unfortunately, that's not terribly helpful in 2E, since the Childer don't really have anything that could be interpreted as a Bloodline Gift. If I were to design them, I'd probably give them some kind of unique fighting style merit. Maybe I'll work something up when I'm more awake...</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the sidebar about them getting the Touch of the Morrigan Cruac Ritual for free would work well in 2e. Just have their Bloodline Gift grant them the ritual automatically, even if they don't have the prerequisite dots in Cruac. Then maybe give them some Bloodline specific Merits or Devotions that synergize with or improve Touch of the Morrigan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T08:43:53-07:00","id":551584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blunt_Force_Trauma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=549638#post549638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking to resurrect the Anubi from Milwaukee by Night into my chronicle of VtR, I see them as a Gangrel bloodline on the interactive character sheet, but no real information in the books I have. I would like to know if they are detailed in any VtR books and if so which one?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the different animal, friend, werewolf-hunting is really not their thing. In fact vampire x werewolf antagonism ain't even a norm/rule like in the old game, doing your own thing from scratch might fit more nicely depending on what you have in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=550265#post550265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the sidebar about them getting the Touch of the Morrigan Cruac Ritual for free would work well in 2e. Just have their Bloodline Gift grant them the ritual automatically, even if they don't have the prerequisite dots in Cruac. Then maybe give them some Bloodline specific Merits or Devotions that synergize with or improve Touch of the Morrigan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can certainly work for the Childer of Morrigan - what is great on itself - but is there any Cruac (or Theban Socery, who knows) ritual that could be interpreted as a Bloodline Gift for the Anubi?<br /> <br /> In Shadows of Mexico there are some interesting tweaks for characters with different animals for Shape of the Beast and those of the condor - vampire may gain 1 Vitae for every 3 points of Size of a carrion corpse for up to 12 hours after its death (+2 on feeding dice pools) \u2014 this doesn\u2019t enable the vampire to feed on creatures below the needs of his Blood Potency - i applied with no qualms to other animals known to feed mostly from carcasses of dead, like vultures, and more importantly in this case, jackals.<br /> <br /> Combo it with the Partial Transformation and you may have a group of jackal &amp;/or vulture-headed undead feeding on corpses as an alternative to preying on the living, in a travestry of actual egyptian worship with the Anubi in a role strongly inspired by the priesthood of Clark Ashton Smith's city of <a href=\"http://www.eldritchdark.com/writings/short-stories/22/the-charnel-god\" target=\"_blank\">Zul-Bha-Sair</a>, for some great imagery for one's games. Even more useful - and gorier - if combined with the liver-eating merit from Mythologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T07:32:34-07:00","id":553019,"title":"","content":"I thought the Anubi get a brief mention in Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T19:13:56-07:00","id":553630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=553019#post553019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Anubi get a brief mention in Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient egypt, certainly, about the Anubi bloodline per se, sparse stuff - most i found was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient Mysteries, pg. 172</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only followers from the cult of <b>Anubis </b>survived, refusing to succumb to invasion and disappear like their brethren. The <b>Anubi</b> would continue to do what they always did, prepare the dead for their journey to the afterlife.<br /> <br /> The <b>Anubi </b>are the only previously known bloodline tocome from the cults of ancient Egypt. Comprised mostly of Gangrel, the Sworn of <b>Anubis </b>have long pestered the followers of Longinus, but have too few numbers, resources and organizational skills to make any kind of impact against the Sanctified. However, word has recently surfaced of two previously unheard of bloodlines claiming to be descendants of the Egyptian gods:</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient Bloodlines, pg. 161</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unity that the Great Covenant brought to Egyptian Kindred and their herds was unparalleled and remained intact for hundreds of years, even after the Greeks invaded the Nile valley. It all came to an end, however, when the Roman Empire, specifically, Ventrue-led Kindred, invaded Egypt and systematically wiped out or sent into hiding the followers of the pantheon of gods. It is believed that several bloodlines were hastily created in order to keep the secrets of the gods hidden from the invaders. The <b>Anubi</b>, <b>a Gangrel-dominated bloodline</b>, claim to be descendants of that time period, while the Circle of the Crone holds within its ranks Kindred who still worship the female gods of Ancient Egypt.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient Bloodlines, pg. 163</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In their efforts to adjust to present time, the Usiri have begun making overtures to their ancient allies, the <b>Anubi</b>, and the re-awakening Bak-Ra, concerning the formation of a pact between their respective bloodlines. Whispers within the Circle of the Crone suggest that they, too, have been contacted by the Sleepers.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ancient Bloodlines, pg. 169</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Servants of Ra disappeared from history and those who have been awakened do not like what they are learning of the past three thousand years. They harbor grudges against their former allies, the Usiri, the <b>Anubi </b>and the other cults of Egypt that still exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall what we get is general confirmation/reinforcement of their bare bones initial presentation in the 1e core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-13-2015, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-15T20:35:22-07:00","id":556432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=550265#post550265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the sidebar about them getting the Touch of the Morrigan Cruac Ritual for free would work well in 2e. Just have their Bloodline Gift grant them the ritual automatically, even if they don't have the prerequisite dots in Cruac. Then maybe give them some Bloodline specific Merits or Devotions that synergize with or improve Touch of the Morrigan.</div> </div> </div> </div>You beat me to it. There was also some sort optional rules for them to work as triumvirate and get a cruac bonus I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-16T13:56:16-07:00","id":557306,"title":"","content":"The ritual power merit for the Children of Morrigan worked like this, any member who had 3 dots of Status (i think crone) could cast as quick action without knowing cruac.<br /> However they did not get the discipline pool bonus in their roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T01:19:44-07:00","id":559137,"title":"","content":"I gave them Auspex and the knowledge of Theban Sorcery (we all know that the Lance had stolen the Sorcery from an Egyptian cult) and a Mystery Cult about guiding Ghosts to eternal peace or destroy them.<br /> <br /> I cant post that unfortunately, because I submitted this version to Onyx Path when they were looking for writers and ideas. I underwrote that I will not publish this. Unfortunately OPP never answered, so my Anubi seem to be lost to the Fog of Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T23:07:17-07:00","id":562674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sethos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/10962-anubi?p=559137#post559137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I gave them Auspex and the knowledge of Theban Sorcery (we all know that the Lance had stolen the Sorcery from an Egyptian cult) and a Mystery Cult about guiding Ghosts to eternal peace or destroy them.<br /> <br /> I cant post that unfortunately, because I submitted this version to Onyx Path when they were looking for writers and ideas. I underwrote that I will not publish this. Unfortunately OPP never answered, so my Anubi seem to be lost to the Fog of Ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bad luck, sometimes it strikes hard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}